.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt NQDCHAIN 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqdchain
.Nd check an append-only chain of capsules
.Sh LIBRARY
libnqd, \-lnqd \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In nqd.h
.Ft int
.Fo nqdchain
.Fa "const char *const *dirs" "size_t n" "const nqcopt *o"
.Fa "uint8_t head[32]" "nqdrep **rep"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A chain is a log of capsules to which a link is only ever added: the
first sealed in format 2, each after it sealed with the one before as
its only input
.Po
.Xr nqseal2 3 ,
.Ql noqtis seal --input
.Pc ,
so that the seal of each signs the id of the last.
.Fn nqdchain
checks the
.Fa n
capsule folders
.Fa dirs ,
oldest first:
.Bl -bullet
.It
each checks as
.Xr nqchkx 3
checks it with
.Fa o
(its trusted key, anchors and key statements;
.Fa o Ns -> Ns Fa only
and
.Fa o Ns -> Ns Fa lin
are not used;
.Fa o
may be
.Dv NULL ) ;
.It
each after the first lists exactly one input, the id
.Pq Xr nqcapid 3
of the one before it, read from its manifest and bound to its seal: the
bytes the seal signs must hash to the capsule's id;
.It
every link is sealed by the key of the first.
.El
.Pp
The first link's own inputs are not followed, so a chain can be checked
from any link on.
Unlike
.Fa o Ns -> Ns Fa lin ,
which follows inputs as a tree to 64 levels, a chain is checked one
link at a time, at any length.
.Pp
The report has a
.Ql link
row per link and per failure, a
.Ql key
row and, when every row passed, a
.Ql head
row with the last link's id in hex, which
.Fa head
then holds; otherwise
.Fa head
is zeros.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv NQOK
when every row passed,
.Dv NQEVRFY
otherwise;
.Fa *rep
is set in both cases
.Pq Xr nqdchk 3 .
.Dv NQEARG
for
.Fa n
0 or a
.Dv NULL
argument;
.Dv NQEMEM .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-chain 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-seal 1 ,
.Xr nqchkx 3 ,
.Xr nqseal2 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
